                <pb facs="0617" n="491" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg491"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">875.01/261: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Albania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grant-Smith</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tirana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-01-25T09:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 25,
                                1925—9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 26—3:20
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>6. Referring to your January 23 [<hi rendition="#italic">22</hi>], 1 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">3</hi>] p.m., number 3. Assembly gave vote of confidence
                    19th. Only British, Greek and Bulgarian representatives having [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">have</hi>] replied to formal notification. French
                    colleague requesting instructions. Italian Minister left on extended leave of
                    absence 18th. Republic proclaimed 21st. All but American representative sent
                    acknowledgment in reply to official notification. Italian Chargé d’Affaires
                    asserts his was noncommittal. Ahmet Bey down with influenza. Will [omission]
                    additional assurances as soon as possible. Copy to European Information
                    Center.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grant-Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
